Expected elements: present

Identity bar (chain exit `← aztec`, truncated hash, `Partial`, both step directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, phase rail), Code pane with line 32 marked, the Call Trace/Event Log tab pair with Call Trace open, Values below it, and the Transaction pane whose first row is `DATA` + `Synthetic demo data` + the producer's sentences — all present. No band above the bar, no spinner, no empty pane.

Typographically the panes are dense and the mono is doing the work it should: the call trace's ACIR column is tabular and right-aligned, the Values pane holds three levels (mono name, mono value, grey type) without a rule between them. The Transaction pane is where the type system thins out.

Worst: the provenance sentences under `DATA` are set right-aligned over eight lines in a ~300 px measure, while the two paragraphs below them in the same pane are left-aligned — the claim the pane exists to carry is the hardest thing on the page to read. Next: one uppercase letterspaced style serves three levels there (`DECODED INPUT` and `EXECUTIONS` are section headings, `BLOCK` and `SELECTOR` are row labels, and nothing separates them). Numbers disagree across panes — `88000 / 200000` unseparated against the call trace's `1,315`. And `Showing from line 26 —` is UI copy set in the code face at code size.

Fixes: left-align the provenance paragraph; give section headings a level of their own.

Rating: 6/10

